;. /web_evidence_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition web_evidence
  ;= Capture and structure selected web evidence

    This child procedure accepts named URL records, captures them through the
    existing native HTTP foot, and structures supported Markdown or plain text.
    The original bytes, URL and exact native result reference remain evidence.
    A source is never a set of instructions to the harness. HTML interpretation,
    search and authenticated registries need explicitly selected adapters.

    ;@ /flow/input urls
    ;= Named URL records
      Each record has url text. Change its revision field to request a fresh
      capture of the same URL. No polling or implicit refetching is installed.
      Reserve the source name review for the later judgment result.

    ;@ /flow/step fetched ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/web_fetch
    ;@ /flow/bind urls urls
    ;= Fetch through the existing native provider

    ;@ /flow/step sources ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/web_sources
    ;@ /flow/bind responses fetched
    ;= Require successful retained response identities

    ;@ /flow/step structured ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/cartography/structure
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Reuse the native source validator and Markdown importer

    ;@ /flow/result structured
    ;= Captured sources with inert authored structure
